/-
# Generators of direct squares of groups without finite quotients (Kourovka Notebook Problem 6.46)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.46 (John S. Wilson): if G is a d-generator
group having no non-trivial finite homomorphic images (in particular, if G is an infinite simple
d-generator group) for some integer d ≥ 2, must G × G be a d-generator group?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Index

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.DirectSquareGeneratorsKourovka6Problem46Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.46 (John S.
Wilson). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700389 (`KOU-6.46`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A `d`-generator group is generated by a set of at most `d` elements. No non-trivial finite
homomorphic image means that every normal subgroup of finite index is the whole group.
-/

/-- Kourovka 6.46 (John S. Wilson): if `d ≥ 2` and `G` is a `d`-generator group with no non-trivial
finite homomorphic images, then `G × G` is a `d`-generator group. -/
def directSquareSameGeneratorNumber : Prop :=
  ∀ d : ℕ, 2 ≤ d → ∀ (G : Type) [Group G],
    (∃ s : Finset G, s.card ≤ d ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set G) = ⊤) →
    (∀ N : Subgroup G, N.Normal → N.FiniteIndex → N = ⊤) →
    ∃ s : Finset (G × G), s.card ≤ d ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set (G × G)) = ⊤

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 6.46 "No, it need not", citing Obraztsov (1993), who
constructs a `2`-generator group `H` without non-trivial finite homomorphic images such that `H × H`
is not `2`-generated (`d(Hⁿ) = 3` for every `n ≥ 2`). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov
(eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49
(2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.46 (John S. Wilson); resolution: V. N. Obraztsov,
Growth sequences of 2-generator simple groups, Proc. Roy. Soc. Edinburgh 123A (1993), 839-855,
zbMATH review Zbl 0814.20024: there is a 2-generator group H having no non-trivial finite
homomorphic images such that d(Hⁿ) = 3 for each n ≥ 2; Kourovka Archive, Problem 6.46: No, it need
not (Obraztsov), https://doi.org/10.1017/S030821050002953X.
-/
public theorem_wanted directSquareSameGeneratorNumber_refuted : ¬ directSquareSameGeneratorNumber

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.DirectSquareGeneratorsKourovka6Problem46Wanted
